<title>NETHERLANDS: AEA overall load factor dips 0.3 pts in '96.</title>
<headline>AEA overall load factor dips 0.3 pts in '96.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The overall load factor for passengers and freight carried by the 26 member airlines of the Association of European Airlines (AEA) fell by 0.3 percentage points to 66.8 percent in 1996, AEA statistics show.</p>
<p>AEA details of the load factors for each airline's scheduled domestic and international routres compared to 1995 included:</p>
<p>    Ranking	    1996	  1995	pt change</p>
<p>96/95</p>
<p>1.  Cargolux	   74.2	  74.6	down  0.4</p>
<p>2.  Air France	 72.7	  70.9	  up  1.8</p>
<p>3.  KLM		  70.9	  73.0	down  2.1</p>
<p>4.  Lufthansa	  70.0	  72.3	down  2.3</p>
<p>5.  Aer Lingus	 69.6	  70.8	down  1.2</p>
<p>6.  Swissair	   69.5	  69.4	  up  0.1</p>
<p>7.  Alitalia	   69.0	  69.2	down  0.2</p>
<p>8.  Sabena	     66.3	  73.1	down  6.8</p>
<p>9.  Icelandair	 65.5	  65.7	down  0.2</p>
<p>10. BA		   65.3	  64.3	  up  1.0</p>
<p>11. Iberia	     61.5	  57.4	  up  4.1</p>
<p>12. Cyprus	     61.3	  58.9	  up  2.4</p>
<p>13. SAS		  59.4	  61.3	down  1.9</p>
<p>14. TAP		  57.8	  59.9	down  2.1</p>
<p>15. Finnair	    55.5	  57.4	down  1.9</p>
<p>16. Austrian	   55.4	  57.3	down  1.9</p>
<p>17. CSA		  54.9	  56.5	down  1.6</p>
<p>18. British Midland  53.6	  54.8	down  1.2</p>
<p>19. Turkish	    53.5	  51.9	  up  1.6</p>
<p>20. Olympic	    52.5	  51.5	  up  1.0</p>
<p>21. Air Malta	  51.7	  46.0	  up  5.7</p>
<p>22. Luxair	     49.7	  50.7	down  1.0</p>
<p>23. JAT		  48.4	  48.7	down  0.3</p>
<p>24. Malev		42.5	  44.4	down  1.9</p>
<p>25. Balkan	     41.1	  42.9	down  1.8</p>
<p>26. Adria Airways    39.4	  40.5	down  1.1</p>
<p>Total AEA airline load factor	    66.8	  67.1	down  0.3</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
